## ffa91bb651d1

**Reproduced advertised-control defect — four helpful controls are inert.**

Generator SHA-256 `b6313c84a93bd8addd04311c398f9aaccc0336c2c3e8dd8def2cc40ad052c2af` declares `palette_kind`, `palette_size`, `n_distinct_colors`, and helpful `texture` values as meaningful axes, but ordinary generation never consumes them. At seed `919100`, sample index `17`, difficulty `medium`, eight invocations spanning warm/cool palette kind, palette size 2/9, distinct-color count 2/9, and warm/cool texture returned byte-identical grids. The chosen input passes `self_check`, and supported Racket application under executed rule hash `021dbc79a954` succeeds.

A 60-sample paired census then found identical outputs in all four comparisons:

- `palette_kind=warm` versus `cool`: 60/60 identical;
- `palette_size=2` versus `9`: 60/60 identical;
- `n_distinct_colors=2` versus `9`: 60/60 identical;
- `texture=warm` versus `cool`: 60/60 identical.

Exact inputs, overrides, hashes, validator result, Racket output, sampler formula, and counts are in `checks/audit/ffa91bb651d1/counterexample.json`. The official linter also reports the missing `RULE_HASH`; strict defect lint independently flags `texture-dead` and `texture-domain-overlap` in `checks/audit/ffa91bb651d1/defect_lint.log`. I am not claiming a separate semantic rule counterexample here—the finding is that the public generator contract promises variation that the sampler does not implement. No target files were changed.
